# Command claude-monitor

## What does this command do:

Real-time monitor of Claude Code token usage and limits, with predictions and warnings.

> Installed via pipx (Python package, version 4.0.0). The same package also
> provides the aliases `ccm`, `ccmonitor`, `claude-code-monitor`, and `cmonitor`
> — all point at the same tool.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: pipx install claude-monitor
For Raspberry Pi install using: sudo apt install pipx  # if pipx is missing, then: pipx install claude-monitor
For Mac install using: brew install pipx && pipx install claude-monitor   # or: uv tool install claude-monitor
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: pipx install claude-monitor

> Note: the Mac container runs Fedora Linux on ARM (aarch64), not x86_64. When a
> package is not installed via `dnf`, download the `aarch64`/`arm64` build of the
> binary — never the `x86_64`/`amd64` build used on the Fedora workstation.
> claude-monitor is a pure-Python package installed via pipx, so no
> architecture-specific build is needed — the same `pipx install` works on aarch64.

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/claude-monitor
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/claude-monitor
For Mac run: ~/.local/bin/claude-monitor
For Mac container run: ~/.local/bin/claude-monitor

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/Maciek-roboblog/Claude-Code-Usage-Monitor

## Command options

```sh
# Run the real-time monitor (default view)
claude-monitor

# Take a single snapshot and exit (no live loop) — handy for scripts
claude-monitor --once

# Choose a plan: pro, max5, max20, team, custom (default: custom)
claude-monitor --plan max20

# Pick a view: realtime, daily, monthly, session, entries, sessions, burn-rate
claude-monitor --view daily

# Structured output for piping: rich (default), json, text, csv
claude-monitor --once --output json

# Only count Anthropic/Claude models (exclude models routed via Claude Code Router)
claude-monitor --filter-models anthropic

# Theme: light, dark, classic, auto (default: auto)
claude-monitor --theme dark

# Plain output, no emoji, no header banner
claude-monitor --no-emoji --no-header

# Run as a Claude Code statusline hook (reads session JSON on stdin)
claude-monitor --statusline

# Set a custom token limit (used with --plan custom)
claude-monitor --plan custom --custom-limit-tokens 500000

# Show version / help
claude-monitor --version
claude-monitor --help
```

Common flags:
- `--plan {pro,max5,max20,team,custom}` — plan type (default: custom)
- `--view {realtime,daily,monthly,session,entries,sessions,burn-rate}` — view mode
- `--once` — measure once, print a snapshot, and exit
- `--output {rich,json,text,csv}` — output format
- `--timezone str` — e.g. `America/New_York` (default: auto)
- `--refresh-rate int` — data refresh in seconds (default: 10)
- `--theme {light,dark,classic,auto}` — display theme
- `--statusline` — one-line status hook for Claude Code
- `--reset-hour {0-23}` — reset hour for daily limits
